{"id": "EUVD-2026-86752", "enisaUuid": "5504b0c1-1e48-3a32-a151-012a44788ad5", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/rockchip: analogix_dp: fix unchecked bound endpoint name length\n\nrockchip_dp_drm_encoder_enable() uses sprintf() to format a device tree\npath into a 32-byte stack buffer. Device tree paths are not limited to\nthis size, so a sufficiently long path can overflow the buffer.\n\nUse snprintf() with the destination size to truncate the generated name\nand keep the writes within bounds.", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:22:26", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:10:24", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/49f5268f43a791dd0d9ff554cce25a3685c7250b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2fcd112caa4ebc64fdcb509f0b26d8daa3fac950", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bc69439d983cc491cc86e01fafc1deb94e1bb85e"], "aliases": ["GHSA-q6xv-ghr2-54fw", "CVE-2026-97621"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "34ff8b3c-43f4-3268-b31f-03ff465322fe", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "729f8eefdcadaff98606931e691910f17d8d59d6 <2fcd112caa4ebc64fdcb509f0b26d8daa3fac950"}, {"id": "5f4f7543-d635-30ad-a84c-054f9754245f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "729f8eefdcadaff98606931e691910f17d8d59d6 <bc69439d983cc491cc86e01fafc1deb94e1bb85e"}, {"id": "76e193bc-8d0e-3490-850a-98ff7865a431", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "844ab939-50dd-3121-85c8-8bdd9c3ffa23", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.16"}, {"id": "92dde11f-17c5-33c7-b6ca-8b432e12c832", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "729f8eefdcadaff98606931e691910f17d8d59d6 <49f5268f43a791dd0d9ff554cce25a3685c7250b"}, {"id": "97daad52-60ae-3211-bf43-43164ffab007", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor"